            "tooltip": {
              "expr": {
                "Literal": {
                  "Value": "'Does a higher cost buy fewer defects?. What it shows: SKUs are grouped by manufacturing cost per unit (low under 34, mid 34 to 67, high 68 and up). Each bar is the group''s average defect rate. How to read it: If the three bars are similar, a higher cost does not buy better quality. The box underneath says it in one sentence.'"
